    "body": "Docs, evidence and one new measurement, on `main` `1be0f8a`, which includes PR #4. No change to `modules/`, the flake, the six checks or `realize.py`.\n\n**Decisions (`nix/sandhi/docs/DECISIONS.md`, all dated 2026-10-05)**\n- F5 deferred, with Tessera's reopening trigger. Mora's lead assignments.\n- DNS review dispositions (Tessera, [`b1b4a20`](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/commit/b1b4a203cfdc051dda693ec54af917c1618ff4b4)). Strict expiry is an objective whose mechanism is unresolved. Publication ordering still needs startup and running-traffic fault tests.\n- Experiment 0's implementation scope, recorded at `ca885b9` before the test existed.\n- Experiment 0's result: the README's limits are corrected, and no mitigation is chosen.\n\n**Experiment 0** (`nix/sandhi/experiments/host-resolution.nix`, evidence in `nix/sandhi/evidence/experiment0-2026-10-05/`)\n- A separate measurement, not a flake check. Its controls gate the run, and each trial is recorded whichever way it falls.\n- Setup: one disposable guest under software emulation, nsncd 1.5.2, and a logging dnsmasq upstream. One attempt; all controls passed.\n- **Finding:** two contracts resolved a name of their own choosing through the host's name-service socket: one with no recipients, and one whose only peer is `127.0.0.2`. The upstream logged each name, sent by the host daemon. The contracts' direct queries were refused. With `/run/nscd` hidden by a test-local override, neither lookup succeeded and nothing reached the upstream.\n- The README no longer says ancillary DNS is \"not silently allowed\" without qualification. It now states that an empty recipient list does not prevent communication carried in DNS queries on such hosts.\n\n**Design and session records**\n- `NAME-RESOLUTION.md`: a reviewed proposal with experiment 0's result. It is not an implementation contract.\n- `SIDEBAND.md`: the start file for a new Sideband session. The routine ID, session ID and cost figure have been removed.\n- `HANDOFF.md`: a prepended checkpoint.\n\n**Publication evidence**\n- `docs/publication/SIDEBAND-ATTRIBUTION-REVIEW-2026-10-05.md` covers what Sideband contributed, material naming Sideband that this runtime can't vouch for (including `boon.html`'s authorship metadata), and items possibly supplied for private development. It also covers third-party material and licensing (GPLv3 alongside the CC BY-SA `boon.html`, and the captured pages and crawl), and a list of decisions for Mora. It is not a full audit.\n- Merge style matters for publication: a squash keeps the removed IDs out of `main` but folds Tessera's commit into one. See section 7 of the review.\n\n**Validation**\n- Each push passed `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` and `python3 anchor.py verify`.\n- Experiment 0 built and passed on this Claude Code container (no KVM). Its output NAR hash is in `SUMMARY.json`.\n- The Sandhi workflow runs the six existing checks, because a file under `nix/sandhi/experiments/` changed. It does not run experiment 0.\n\nDiscussion: [PR #5 thread](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/pull/5#issuecomment-5986420376). There is no archived context manifest, so this is a declared gap. Merging and the visibility change are Mora's decisions.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015f2oo3zcddjSg7k3FsoRgS",
